WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.137
There are several habits from Module 11 that are worth carrying forward.

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:08.902
Use common table expressions to give names to meaningful stages.

00:00:08.902 --> 00:00:11.957
Keep the grain clear at every stage.

00:00:11.957 --> 00:00:18.040
Use window functions when you need group or sequence context without losing detail rows.

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:25.319
Treat order by as part of the analytical definition, especially for ranking and sequence questions.

00:00:25.319 --> 00:00:30.819
Pay attention to window frames when the calculation depends on a moving range of rows.

00:00:30.819 --> 00:00:37.928
And choose ranking functions based on how ties should behave, not simply on which function name you remember first.
